※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1
※ pl4g-test: run=native,qemu exit=5
※ pl4g-test: diag=none

※ `&` binds tighter than `^`, which binds tighter than `|`, as in C and every
※ language that followed it.  Read as 1 | (6 ^ (3 & 2)), which is 5; read the
※ other way round it would be 0.
@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    1u6 | 6u6 ^ 3u6 & 2u6
